From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: hy200-qz713df-a1: power-off cuts the core rails

OUT OF SERIES -- NEGATIVE RESULT (2026-10-07). Driving PL6 low does not keep
the board off: it REBOOTS it. Tested live on the bench board (filesystems
synced and remounted read-only first): the core rails collapse, the SoC
resets, PL6 returns to its reset default, the rails come back with mains
still present, and the serial console shows U-Boot SPL starting again. Stock
can use PL6 for "super standby" only because the ARISC, on the standby rail,
holds it low; with no ARISC firmware nothing survives the reset to do that.
With this patch, poweroff would reboot. Kept for the record.

poweroff never turned the board off. The only handler was PSCI SYSTEM_OFF,
and this BL31 implements it by parking the CPUs: the power LED stays blue,
the lamp and fan keep running and the panel holds the last frame
(operator-observed 2026-10-07, after logind powered off on KEY_POWER).

There is no PMIC. Stock's standby_param names PL6 as the enable for
vdd-cpu, vdd-sys, vcc-pll and vcc-dram, and U-Boot leaves it an output,
driven high. Describe it as a gpio-poweroff line, active low, so the end of
poweroff drops the SoC's core rails and only a power cycle brings it back.

Priority 255 makes it run before PSCI's handler (SYS_OFF_PRIO_FIRMWARE + 2),
which never returns. The line is requested inactive (high), so probe leaves
the rails alone.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -38,6 +38,23 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Real power-off. PL6 enables the SoC's core rails: stock's
+	 * standby_param names it for vdd-cpu, vdd-sys, vcc-pll and vcc-dram,
+	 * and U-Boot leaves it an output, high. Dropping it at the end of
+	 * poweroff takes the SoC down for good -- only a power cycle brings it
+	 * back. Priority 255 runs it before PSCI SYSTEM_OFF (firmware + 2),
+	 * which on this BL31 only parks the CPUs with the rails, the lamp and
+	 * the last frame still up. Requested inactive, so nothing changes at
+	 * probe.
+	 */
+	poweroff {
+		compatible = "gpio-poweroff";
+		gpios = <&r_pio 0 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PL6 */
+		priority = <255>;
+		timeout-ms = <1000>;
+	};
+
 	h713-edid-clock-hold {
 		compatible = "h713-lab,edid-clock-hold";
 		clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_R_EDID>;
